From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: draws with an out-of-range shape type or index format are skipped, table reads clamped (EDEN_UP_DRAW_ENUM_GUARD), off by default

What: a safety net under the first-start crash of 12 Nov (junk command words stored shape type
3734, a texture draw followed, UpdateDepthBiasEnable read POLYGON_OFFSET_ENABLE_LUT[3734]: SIGSEGV
on GPUBack). New header video_core/draw_enum_guard.h (mode, counters, lines, Bad(), TableIndex(),
Tick()). With EDEN_UP_DRAW_ENUM_GUARD=2: ProcessDraw and ProcessDrawIndirect (right after
UpdateTopology) skip a draw whose shape type is above 14 or (indexed) whose index format is above
2, and set the stored shape type to Triangles; DrawTexture resets a bad stored shape type to
Triangles and goes ahead; the topology_override default branch ignores values above 14 and keeps
the draw begin's shape type; IndexBuffer::FormatSizeInBytes returns 1 for a bad format instead of
UNREACHABLE (abort); the four table reads (vk_rasterizer.cpp UpdateDepthBiasEnable,
fixed_pipeline_state.cpp TOPOLOGY_CLASS_REPRESENTATIVE_LUT, Refresh2 POLYGON_OFFSET_ENABLE_LUT,
UnpackCullFace) use the Triangles (or Back) entry for an index past their end.

Switch: EDEN_UP_DRAW_ENUM_GUARD, read once at first use: unset or 0 the old code; 1 count and log
every out-of-range value, change nothing (the table reads still read outside: count on healthy
streams only); 2 act; anything else DefaultMode (0 now) with one warning line (an empty value
also warns).
Log (LOG_INFO, HW_GPU): first use "EDEN_UP_DRAW_ENUM_GUARD=2: a draw with an out-of-range shape
type or index format is skipped, table reads use the Triangles entry" (=1 "... are counted,
nothing changed"); each value seen (first 200, then one "further lines left out" line)
"EDEN_UP_DRAW_ENUM_GUARD #1: draw shape type = 3734 (0xe96, valid 0-14): draw skipped, stored shape
type set to Triangles" (sites: draw shape type, indirect draw shape type, texture draw stored shape
type, shape type override, draw index format, index format size, depth bias table (dynamic), depth
bias table (pipeline), pipeline shape class table, packed cull face; =1 "count only, nothing
changed"); every 10 s (clock read every 1024 draws, totals since boot, zeros included)
"EDEN_UP_DRAW_ENUM_GUARD 10s: mode 2, N draws seen; out of range since boot: draw shape 0, ...;
draws skipped 0, values replaced 0". A hung run stops printing the 10 s line (it comes from draws).

Not in TranslationSwitches: pipeline keys of valid streams are unchanged.

Cost when off: one cached-static test per draw and per texture draw, one always-true compare at
each of the four table reads; nothing on the index size path. Behaviour the same (the old path at
those reads is undefined behaviour anyway), machine code not. maxwell_3d.h now includes the new
header (wide recompile; one inline counter object of about 120 bytes).

Default flip (later): video_core/draw_enum_guard.h "inline constexpr int DefaultMode = 0;" -> 2;
=0 stays the escape hatch. Only after the cold runs that had junk show no crash at the table and
hangs no more often than reaching the house (a crash restarts the app by itself, a hang does not).

Risks: a game that really sends a shape type above 14 would lose those draws (none known; =1
checks Ocarina); with the crash gone the junk stream goes on and may hang; a junk override with a
valid begin shape type draws with the begin's shape type instead of being skipped.

Origin and credit: our own work, no upstream source. Draft
drafts-2026-11-11/ports-7/first-start/topology-guard/draft.diff, placed unchanged (review: ready to
place, default stays off).
---
